Two issues:

1. The input has no associated label; a `<div>` and placeholder do not provide a reliable accessible name.
2. “Optional” has insufficient contrast: `#aaa` on white is approximately 2.32:1, below the 4.5:1 requirement for normal text.

```html
<div class="note-field">
  <label for="internal-note">Internal note</label>
  <p id="note-hint" class="hint">Optional</p>
  <input
    id="internal-note"
    name="internal-note"
    type="text"
    aria-describedby="note-hint"
  >
  <button type="button">Save</button>
</div>
```

```css
.note-field {
  max-width: 30rem;
  color: #222;
  background: #fff;
}

.note-field label {
  display: block;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.hint {
  margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  color: #595959;
}

.note-field input,
.note-field button {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
  font: inherit;
  color: #222;
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #767676;
}

.note-field input {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}

.note-field :is(input, button):focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #005fcc;
  outline-offset: 3px;
}
```

The button remains static and does not submit or save anything.
